# per-leaf-manifest — ALLOW-LIST for verify-merged per-leaf suite filter (issue #194)
#
# Format:
#   ALLOW    <basename>  — leaf-unit-safe; included in per-leaf verify-merged
#   EXCLUDED <basename>  — heavy/timing/process; GHA full suite only (ci.yml:21-33)
#
# Criterion ALLOW (fail-safe): verdict = pure function of merged content only.
#   No launcher loops, no background processes, no timing/poll/sleep asserts,
#   no recursive verify-merged calls.  Any doubt ⇒ EXCLUDED (fail-closed default).
#
# Guard invariant (fail-closed):
#   ALLOW ∪ EXCLUDED == all reference/tests/*.test.sh   (union is complete)
#   ALLOW ∩ EXCLUDED == ∅                               (disjoint)
#   Any unclassified *.test.sh ⇒ guard RED.
#   To add a test to ALLOW you MUST document it here with a criterion justification.
#
# Counts: ALLOW=16, EXCLUDED=40, union=56  (verify with: leaf-verifier.test.sh Test 7)
#
# #206 Part B: runtime-manifest promoted EXCLUDED→ALLOW. Its verdict is a pure
#   function of merged content (sha256 / find / awk / grep — no launcher loop, no
#   background process, no timing/poll/sleep, no recursive verify-merged), so it
#   meets the ALLOW criterion. Promotion is SOUND only because verify-merged
#   regenerates the sha-lock IN-CLONE before the gate suite (#206 Part A): without
#   that, benign sha-drift would false-RED Test 3; with it, Test 3 stays green on
#   drift while Test 1/2/4 still catch structural breaks (missing row / removed
#   runtime file / wrong status). This also retires the #130 flake (transient
#   drift-fail) for the per-leaf gate.
# #206 also adds charter-finale-regen (the A-persistence integration test): heavy
#   git (clone/merge/push to prove persistence on MAIN) ⇒ EXCLUDED. union 45→46.

